url: "https://github.com/xmpuspus/kb-arena"
license: MIT
version: "0.9.0"
date-released: "2026-06-22"
abstract: >
  KB Arena benchmarks eleven retrieval architectures (naive vector, contextual
  vector, QnA pairs, knowledge graph, hybrid via reciprocal rank fusion,
  RAPTOR, PageIndex, BM25, rerank-vector, plus two quantum rerankers — QISS, a
  quantum-inspired state-fidelity reranker, and SQR, a Qiskit Aer SWAP-test
  reranker) head-to-head on user-provided documentation. It auto-generates
  benchmark questions across five difficulty tiers, computes a layered IR metric
  stack (Recall@k, Precision@k, Hit@k, MRR, NDCG@k, MAP, R-Precision, bpref)
  with bootstrap 95% confidence intervals, supports graded NDCG with exponential
  gain, includes a Rank-Biased Overlap implementation for strategy-vs-strategy
  comparison, and ships an automated hyperparameter search (kb-arena optimize)
  that reports Wilcoxon paired significance tests, win-rate, and a Pareto
  frontier over the (quality, latency) plane.
